    content: `Construction in flood prone areas of Sri Lanka requires special measures. Identify flood risk level of the site from local authority maps and historical flood records. Raise floor level minimum 600mm above the 100 year flood level. Construct building on elevated platform or plinth. Use flood resistant materials at lower levels including concrete and ceramic tiles rather than timber and carpet. Install flood doors or barriers at entrances. Electrical panel and sockets should be above flood level, minimum 1.5 meters above floor. Waterproof lower walls to 600mm above anticipated flood level. Provide sump pump to remove flood water from basement or low areas. Flood vents in foundation walls allow water to flow through and equalize pressure reducing structural damage. Landscaping with rain gardens and permeable paving reduces surface runoff. Consider flood insurance as standard property insurance may exclude flood damage. Colombo suburban areas of Kelani River valley and coastal lowlands are high flood risk.`
